= Perception — Technical =

== Inverse problem ==
Perceptual systems often solve an underdetermined inverse problem:

<pre>
distal world state
      ↓
proximal sensory signal

perception estimates:
sensory signal → likely world state
</pre>

Many different world states can produce similar sensory input.

== Psychophysics ==
Psychophysics relates physical stimulus variables to perceptual responses.

Signal detection theory separates sensitivity from decision criterion, preventing response bias from being mistaken for sensory ability.

== Bayesian formulation ==
Some models describe perception as inference:

<pre>
P(world | signal) ∝ P(signal | world) P(world)
</pre>

This does not imply that people consciously perform Bayesian calculations.

== Predictive and ecological approaches ==
Predictive approaches emphasize top-down prediction and prediction error.

Ecological approaches emphasize information available in structured organism–environment relations and may reject stronger inferential assumptions.

